{"availability":"available","full":"julienR2/jarvis","name":"jarvis","description":"A self-hosted AI assistant that can rewrite its own code — Claude Code CLI behind a chat UI, with crons, webhooks, connectors and generated apps.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-15T23:22:26Z","updated":"2026-10-08T23:30:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://julienr2.github.io/jarvis/","topics":["ai-agent","ai-assistant","anthropic","automation","chatbot","claude","claude-code","docker","fastify","llm","personal-assistant","pwa","react","self-hosted","typescript"],"demo":"https://julienr2.github.io/jarvis/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T14:53:14.065Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T14:53:14.065Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T14:53:14.065Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T14:53:14.065Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A self-hosted AI assistant that can rewrite its own code.","Jarvis is a web chat interface backed by the Claude Code CLI. What separates it from other chat wrappers: the assistant has full read/write access to its own source code. Ask it to add a feature, fix a bug, or build an integration — it edits the frontend and backend directly, and you review, commit, or revert every change through git.","The idea is less \"deploy and use\" and more \"deploy and shape.\" You start with a general-purpose assistant and vibe-code it into something personal."],"features":["It edits itself. Not a plugin API, not a config file — the agent opens your actual source, changes it, and the container rebuilds. Git is the safety net.","It runs without you. Crons and webhooks fire the agent on a schedule or an HTTP call, with full conversation context. Your assistant keeps working while you sleep.","It reaches your things. Connectors put real credentials — Gmail, GitHub, Slack, Linear, whatever you add — in the agent's hands at runtime, no code and no restart."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/julienR2/jarvis/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"48318eccdec0bcc0ec72925b5345bf64c5d4e2d79eb297f6f7808e3aaa8ee11b","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T14:53:14.232Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T14:53:14.232Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A self-hosted AI assistant that can rewrite its own code.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/julienR2/jarvis/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"A self-hosted AI assistant that can rewrite its own code.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/julienR2/jarvis/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Some things can't be fetched, they have to be clicked — a site behind a login, a flow with no API.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/julienR2/jarvis/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Headless has a limit: it can't solve a captcha or take a login you'd rather type yourself.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/julienR2/jarvis/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Open The first visit walks you through the rest: create your account, then paste a Claude OAuth token (the wizard shows how to get one with claude setup-token — requires a Claude subscription).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/julienR2/jarvis/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"48318eccdec0bcc0ec72925b5345bf64c5d4e2d79eb297f6f7808e3aaa8ee11b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/julienR2/jarvis/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T14:53:14.233Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T23:30:50Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/julienR2/jarvis/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T14:53:14.234Z","hash":"48318eccdec0bcc0ec72925b5345bf64c5d4e2d79eb297f6f7808e3aaa8ee11b","originalBytes":17673,"storedBytes":17673,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["agent","claude","jarvis","code","model",